%% DM26-0670

%% An agent holds a problem a restart would not help, and a signed update mends it, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/soft-state.md, "A held agent tries
%% again on a signed update", docs/architecture/jira.md, "What it does at start"). jira-observer is the one user. How the document gets there is
%% general/signed_configuration_delivery, and after a restart general/configuration_replay. What the health actor answers is general/pulled_health.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Author as Author (polar-sign)
    participant Config as ConfigurationActor
    participant Held as HeldSupervisor
    participant Try as TryAgain<br/>(the agent's closure)
    participant Work as the agent's work
    participant Health as HealthCheckActor
    participant Writer as soft-state-processor

    Note over Held,Try: The render passed it, and the agent's own judgment refuses it<br/>(prepare: the placeholder address, a date that does not parse)
    Held->>Held: held::stay_up: build the infrastructure, and no domain
    Held->>Health: hold(Configuration, what to set)
    Note over Health: A hold never becomes a verdict. The file says unhealthy,<br/>the probe judges only its age, and it rejuvenates<br/>as any agent does, so the pod's rule has no loop to run
    Held->>Config: subscribe to changes()
    Writer->>Health: asked, at each round
    Health-->>Writer: Unhealthy, reason configuration, and the message

    Author->>Config: a signed configuration document, by delivery or replay
    Config->>Config: verify, then apply_overrides: only a Dynamic variable, all or none
    alt nothing changed, or it was refused
        Note over Config: No announcement. The outcome says why, and the hold stands
    else a value changed
        Config-)Held: ConfigChanged { version, changed }
        Held->>Config: current()
        Config-->>Held: the configuration in force
        Held->>Try: Retry { config, resources, supervisor, cassini_registered }
        alt it still cannot work
            Try-->>Held: Err(why)
            Held->>Health: hold(Configuration, why), the new message
        else it can
            Try->>Work: start, linked under the held supervisor, on the infrastructure already built
            Try-->>Held: Ok
            Held->>Health: release(Configuration)
            Note over Held,Work: From here the work takes the agent's events and answers the shutdown,<br/>and its ending ends the agent
        end
    end

    Note over Config,Work: Once the work runs, a Dynamic change goes to it (jira-observer's supervisor, for a setting that touches the observers)
    Config-)Work: ConfigChanged { version, changed }
    Work->>Config: current()
    Work->>Work: prepare() on it
    alt the settings work
        Work->>Work: stop the observers, and start them with the new settings
        Work->>Health: release every hold (an observer that meets it again holds it again)
    else they cannot
        Work->>Work: stop the observers
        Work->>Health: hold(Configuration, why), until an update mends it
    end

    alt told to end while held, with no work running
        Held->>Held: PrepareShutdown: nothing to finish, ProceedWithShutdown at once
    end
